-- ============================================================================
-- e2e-fixtures.sql — Test-only seed for E2E test classes
-- ============================================================================
--
-- Applied via @Sql(scripts = "/db/seed/e2e-fixtures.sql",
--                  executionPhase = BEFORE_TEST_METHOD) on the three E2E test
-- classes (OnlineTransactionE2ETest, AdminUserManagementE2ETest,
-- GateVerificationE2ETest). BEFORE_TEST_METHOD (rather than the more efficient
-- BEFORE_TEST_CLASS) is required because BEFORE_TEST_CLASS fires from
-- SpringExtension.beforeAll BEFORE the TestcontainersExtension has started the
-- @Container PostgreSQLContainer — at which point the @DynamicPropertySource
-- lambda binding {@code spring.datasource.url} to {@code POSTGRES::getJdbcUrl}
-- throws "Mapped port can only be obtained after the container is started"
-- during context load. BEFORE_TEST_METHOD defers script execution until after
-- all @BeforeAll hooks complete (container started, context refreshed,
-- DataSource resolved). Per-method invocation overhead is minimal because every
-- INSERT carries ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING (see idempotency note below).
--
-- NOT a Flyway migration — placed under
-- src/test/resources/db/seed/ (not src/main/resources/db/migration/) so it
-- does NOT execute automatically on every @SpringBootTest context load. This
-- decouples the E2E test data from the production V3__seed.sql (which now
-- carries ONLY canonical reference data: 7 transaction_types,
-- 18 transaction_categories, 51 discount_groups) so that:
--   1. Repository ITs (CustomerRepositoryIT, CardRepositoryIT,
--      AccountRepositoryIT, CardXrefRepositoryIT, UserSecurityRepositoryIT,
--      etc.) which INSERT their own synthetic records under IDs like
--      000000010, 000000050, 4111111111111101, USRTST01, ADMTST01 are
--      NOT blocked by pre-existing PK rows seeded by V3. Per AAP §0.10
--      "test isolation" each IT controls its own data lifecycle via
--      @DataJpaTest's @Transactional rollback.
--   2. E2E tests (which DO need the customer/account/card/transaction
--      lookup state to be populated before sign-on) receive the full
--      50-record fixture set via @Sql application BEFORE the test class
--      runs.
--
-- The script is IDEMPOTENT — every INSERT carries ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
-- so re-applying the script (e.g., on @Sql executionPhase=BEFORE_TEST_METHOD
-- if a future test class needs per-method re-seeding) is safe. The
-- ON CONFLICT clause also lets multiple E2E test classes share the same
-- seed state without cleanup ordering concerns.
--
-- Source-of-truth fixtures: app/data/ASCII/{custdata,acctdata,carddata,
-- cardxref,dailytran}.txt mirrored under src/test/resources/baseline/input/.
-- Records emitted by /tmp/build_seed.py with COBOL zoned-decimal sign
-- overpunch conversion (POSITIVE_OVERPUNCH / NEGATIVE_OVERPUNCH).
--
-- Counts: 2 security_users + 50 customers + 50 accounts + 50 cards
--         + 50 card_xref + 50 transactions.
--
-- Insert order respects foreign-key dependencies even though no FK
-- constraints are declared in V1__schema.sql:
--   security_users (independent)
--   -> customers (independent)
--   -> accounts (denormalised customer_id from cardxref)
--   -> cards (card_acct_id references accounts)
--   -> card_xref (xref_card_num, xref_acct_id reference cards/accounts)
--   -> transactions (card_number references cards)
--
-- BCrypt hashes embedded below correspond to
-- TestFixtures.Users.TEST_PASSWORD_PLAINTEXT (the canonical fixture
-- plaintext value); production-side BCrypt verification round-trips
-- these hashes against the plaintext per AAP §0.10.5.
-- ============================================================================


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 5. customers (50 rows from app/data/ASCII/custdata.txt)
--    Layout per app/cpy/CUSTREC.cpy: 500-byte fixed-width record
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 6. accounts (50 rows from app/data/ASCII/acctdata.txt)
--    Layout per app/cpy/CVACT01Y.cpy: 300-byte fixed-width record
--    customer_id is denormalised via app/data/ASCII/cardxref.txt (1:1 in fixtures)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 7. cards (50 rows from app/data/ASCII/carddata.txt)
--    Layout per app/cpy/CVACT02Y.cpy: 150-byte fixed-width record
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 8. card_xref (50 rows from app/data/ASCII/cardxref.txt)
--    Layout per app/cpy/CVACT03Y.cpy: 50-byte fixed-width record
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 9. transactions (50 rows from app/data/ASCII/dailytran.txt)
--    Layout per app/cpy/CVTRA05Y.cpy: 350-byte fixed-width record
--    First 50 of 300 daily transactions are seeded as a representative subset
--    sufficient for online list/detail endpoints and E2E sign-on flows.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
